<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">19</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pressburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-pressburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pressburg</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 907</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pressburg was fought on 4 July 907 near Pressburg, modern Bratislava, when a Hungarian army destroyed a large Bavarian force under Margrave Luitpold, who…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-achelous"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-achelous.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Achelous</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 917</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Achelous was fought on 20 August 917 by the river Achelous, near Anchialus on the Black Sea coast of present-day Bulgaria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-katasyrtai"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Katasyrtai</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 917</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Katasyrtai was fought in 917 near Constantinople, shortly after Simeon I's victory at Achelous.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-valdejunquera"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-valdejunquera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Valdejunquera</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 920</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Valdejunquera was fought on 26 July 920 in Navarre.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-riade"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-riade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Riade</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 933</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Riade was fought in March 933, probably near the Unstrut river in Thuringia, between King Henry the Fowler of East Francia and a Magyar raiding army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-illicheon"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Illicheon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 936</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Illicheon was fought in 936 near Gumi in Korea, when Wang Geon, founder of Goryeo, defeated the army of Later Baekje led by Gyeon Singeom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunanburh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunanburh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Brunanburh</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 937</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Brunanburh was fought in 937 between Æthelstan, king of the English, and an alliance of Olaf Guthfrithson, king of Dublin, Constantine II of Scotland and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-andernach"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Andernach</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 939</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Andernach was fought on 2 October 939 on the Rhine near Andernach.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-simancas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-simancas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Simancas</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 939</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Simancas was fought in August 939 near Simancas on the Pisuerga, close to the Douro, between Ramiro II of León and the army of Abd al-Rahman III, caliph…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-trans"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Trans</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 939</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Trans was fought in 939 at Trans, near Dol in north-eastern Brittany, traditionally on 1 August.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-takkolam"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Takkolam</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 949</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Takkolam was fought in 949 near Takkolam, north-west of Kanchipuram in present-day Tamil Nadu, between the Rashtrakuta emperor Krishna III, allied with…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaoping"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gaoping</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 954</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gaoping was fought in 954 in Shanxi, northern China, between the Later Zhou under Emperor Chai Rong and the Northern Han allied with the Khitan Liao.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Lechfeld</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 955 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Lechfeld was fought in 955 CE near Augsburg, where Otto I of Saxony decisively defeated the invading Magyars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sulcoit"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sulcoit</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 967</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sulcoit was fought in 967 near the town of Tipperary in Munster, Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaoliang-river"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gaoliang River</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 979</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gaoliang River was fought in 979 near modern Beijing between the Song emperor Taizong and the army of the Liao dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-torrevicente"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Torrevicente</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 981</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Torrevicente was fought in 981 in the province of Soria, Spain, between the Córdoban general Almanzor and his father-in-law Ghalib, who had rebelled…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fyrisvellir"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fyrisvellir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Fýrisvellir</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 985</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Fýrisvellir was fought in the 980s on the plains near Uppsala, where King Eric the Victorious of the Swedes defeated his nephew Styrbjörn the Strong, who…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-conquereuil"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Conquereuil</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 992</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Conquereuil was fought in 992 near Conquereuil in eastern Brittany, north of Nantes, between Conan I of Rennes, who claimed the rule of all Brittany, and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-spercheios"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-spercheios.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Spercheios</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 997</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Spercheios was fought in 997 on the river Spercheios in central Greece.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-dorostolon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-dorostolon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Dorostolon</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 971</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Dorostolon took place from April to July 971 at Dorostolon, now Silistra, on the lower Danube.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-capture-of-damascus"><span class="enc-name">Fatimid capture of Damascus</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 978</span><span class="enc-snip">The Fatimid capture of Damascus in 978 brought the city under the control of the Fatimid Caliphate after years of conflict with local forces and rivals.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/capture-of-awdaghast-992"><span class="enc-name">Capture of Awdaghast (992)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 992 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The capture of Awdaghast in 992 CE was the conquest by the Ghana Empire of the oasis town of Awdaghast, previously held by Zanata Berbers.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-bulgarian-war-of-913-927"><span class="enc-name">Byzantine–Bulgarian war of 913–927</span><span class="enc-type">War · 913–927</span><span class="enc-snip">The Byzantine–Bulgarian war of 913–927 was fought between the Bulgarian Empire under Simeon I and the Byzantine Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslavs-campaign-against-the-khazars"><span class="enc-name">Sviatoslav's campaign against the Khazars</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 960s</span><span class="enc-snip">Sviatoslav's campaign against the Khazars was a series of military expeditions by the prince of Kievan Rus in the 960s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-conquest-of-bulgaria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-conquest-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Byzantine conquest of Bulgaria</span><span class="enc-type">War · 968–1018</span><span class="enc-snip">The Byzantine conquest of Bulgaria was the series of wars from 968 to 1018 in which the Byzantine Empire destroyed the First Bulgarian Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslavs-invasion-of-bulgaria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sviatoslavs-invasion-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sviatoslav's invasion of Bulgaria</span><span class="enc-type">War · 968–971</span><span class="enc-snip">Sviatoslav's invasion of Bulgaria was the campaign of 968–971 in which Sviatoslav I of Kiev, first invited by the Byzantines, conquered much of the First Bulgarian…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-conquest-of-egypt"><span class="enc-name">Fatimid conquest of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 969 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Fatimid conquest of Egypt in 969 CE was led by the general Jawhar al-Siqilli, who took the country with little resistance from the weakened Ikhshidid regime.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/srivijayan-invasion-of-medang"><span class="enc-name">Srivijayan invasion of Medang</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 990 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Srivijayan invasion of Medang was a military campaign by Srivijaya against the Javanese kingdom of Medang in 990 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/chola-chalukya-wars"><span class="enc-name">Chola–Chalukya wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · c. 992–1120</span><span class="enc-snip">The Chola–Chalukya wars were a long series of conflicts in the 11th and early 12th centuries between the Chola dynasty of the Tamil country and the Western Chalukyas of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/goryeo-khitan-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/goryeo-khitan-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Goryeo–Khitan War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 993–1019</span><span class="enc-snip">The Goryeo–Khitan War was a series of invasions of the Korean kingdom of Goryeo by the Khitan Liao dynasty between 993 and 1019.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chenqiao-mutiny"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/chenqiao-mutiny.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chenqiao Mutiny</span><span class="enc-type">Revolution · 960 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Chenqiao Mutiny was the coup of 960 CE in which troops of the Later Zhou commander Zhao Kuangyin draped him in the imperial yellow robe and proclaimed him emperor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Great Slav Rising</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 983</span><span class="enc-snip">The Great Slav Rising was a revolt of the Polabian Slavs, led by the Lutician tribes, against German rule east of the Elbe in 983.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Treaties <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-clair-sur-epte"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-clair-sur-epte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 911</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, traditionally dated to 911, was an agreement between the West Frankish king Charles the Simple and the Viking leader Rollo.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Peace efforts &amp; congresses <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/council-of-charroux"><span class="enc-name">Council of Charroux</span><span class="enc-type">Peace · 989</span><span class="enc-snip">The Council of Charroux was a church synod held in 989 at the abbey of Charroux in Poitou, convened by Archbishop Gunbald of Bordeaux.</span></a></li></ul></section>
